{
  "_about": "Hair, one category drawn in two layers. This file (09-front-hair) is the listing of record: every hair id, in builder order. 02-back-hair/_meta.json lists the same ids for the ones that also draw behind the neck. \"layers\" says where each id draws; bald draws nothing.",
  "crown": "Each part also carries data-crown on its SVG root: the y, in the 256 viewBox, of the top of the hair at the centre line. Headwear with data-anchor=\"crown\" (the kippah) is moved down by (crown - 60). With no hair part drawn, crown is 62.",
  "colorFrom": "The hijab takes a clothing color, not a hair color: its {{hair}} and {{hairShade}} slots are filled from palette.clothing[hairColor] (as source/lib/compose-core.mjs does for hairColorFrom \"clothing\"). Brows under a hijab still take a hair color (dark brown by default).",
  "buzz": "buzz, top-knot (sides) and shaved-side (one side) draw hair at opacity 0.62 so the skin shows through, as a clipped cut does.",
